OL,3,GNEWSAPrime minister visits Aberfan
OL,4,Aahead of 60th anniversary of
OL,5,A'horrifying tragedy'
OL,6,
OL,7,FPrime Minister Andy Burnham has visited
OL,8,FAberfan ahead of the Welsh mining
OL,9,Fvillage marking 60 years since a coal
OL,10,Fwaste tip collapsed and engulfed a
OL,11,Fschool, killing 144 children and
OL,12,Fadults.
OL,14,FBurnham laid a wreath at the memorial
OL,15,Fgarden on Monday, alongside survivor
OL,16,FJeff Edwards, who was one of the last
OL,17,Fchildren to be brought out alive from
OL,18,Fthe rubble, and Welsh Secretary Stephen
OL,19,FKinnock.
OL,23,APub: 19-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
FL,439,430,260,140,0,100
